// The Quiet Woods: an example game that comes with the engine.
//
// Every file shows one part of the content format in small, working form, with
// comments that explain the fields. README.md has a map of which feature lives
// in which file. template.fsc holds the common definitions, ready to copy.
//
// To start your own game: copy this folder, rename it, change the ID below
// (and in nothing else), then change anything you like.

== pack example-adventure
name: Example adventure
version: 0.2.0
authors: MAGE project
// The pack that is the game sets the main menu: title, subtitle and footer.
// It may also name a logo, a background and `menu icons` from its images folder.
title: The Quiet Woods
subtitle: An example adventure
about: A tiny example game that comes with the engine. Copy its pack folder to start your own.
// A game may also show a notice each time it starts, with an OK button
// (`start notice title:` and a long `start notice:` with **bold**, *italic* and
// web addresses as links), and give `feedback webhook:` a Discord webhook address
// that the Report a bug / Feedback button sends players' reports to. Without one,
// the report window says that reports cannot be sent yet. `feedback receiver:` is
// an address of your own (a tracker's intake) that gets the whole report as JSON:
// only with one can a player add the state of the game and a save to a report.
// For example:
//
// start notice title: Welcome
// start notice:
//     This is a test build. Tell us what you think with the Report a bug button.
// feedback webhook: PASTE-WEBHOOK-URL-HERE
// feedback receiver: PASTE-WEBHOOK-URL-HERE
